A||||13||Cheever3000||What happened at the Pegasus Ranch?||||6||
Z||000000||Cheever3000||09-05-2001||10:12 PM||||That could be the “Who shot J.R.” question on the Fiero Forum.  Unfortunately, most of you won’t know what I’m talking about.  In due time, you will.  But I’m posting this to thank the magnificent few who accepted my invitation, and helped me build a dream by turning a desolate prairie into the Pontiac Ponderosa.  The gunslingers, cowgirls, dudes and wranglers who strapped on their spurs to ride with me, gave my spirit a lift on the wind of adventure.  They came together to rescue the wagon train in distress, but then discovered another renegade outfit had already formed a posse.  Relieved that the trail is open again to the promise of a new frontier, we sit tall in our saddles knowing we were there to help save the settlers and see history in the making.  As you each ride out across the horizon into the sunset, I tip my hat to you.  Thanks, pardners!  The gates of Pegasus Ranch will always be open to ya.<P>Rancher Chuck<P>Cliff:  Please keep this in the General section.  I’d like for it to be archived forever.  Believe it or not, it really is Fiero related.<BR>||||reg||6
